# Frontend (Next.js)

Call chain:

```text
page (server) → lib/ helper → data
page → component → components/ui primitive
route handler → lib/ helper (thin)
```

- Pages compose components and fetch via `lib/` helpers — keep business logic out of markup-heavy pages.
- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only at the smallest interactive subtree.
- Client code must not import server-only helpers (DB pool, secrets, Node-only modules).
- Route handlers stay thin and call one helper.

**Naming:** folders `kebab-case`; components `PascalCase`; helpers `*.ts`.

**Split when:** page > ~80 lines, component > ~150 lines, or mixed data + markup. Extract loading/empty/error into sibling components.

**Split shape:** once a route needs splitting, colocate per-route:

```text
app/<route>/
  page.tsx                server: data fetching + composition only
  types.ts                view-level types for this route
  hooks/
    use-*.ts              client hooks ("use client")
  components/
    *.tsx                 server or client components scoped to this route
```

- `hooks/` is for client-only logic — never fetch data or call DB code from inside a hook.
- Server-only data fetching stays in `page.tsx` or a route-scoped server component under `components/`.
- Top-level `components/` and `lib/` are for pieces shared across multiple routes.
